      "text": "To find out how many minutes it will take to print 200 pages, we can use the information that the printer prints 17 pages per minute. We can set up a proportion to solve for the time \\( t \\) in minutes:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{17 \\text{ pages}}{1 \\text{ minute}} = \\frac{200 \\text{ pages}}{t \\text{ minutes}}\n\\]\n\nTo solve for \\( t \\), we can cross-multiply:\n\n\\[\n17t = 200\n\\]\n\nThen, divide both sides by 17 to isolate \\( t \\):\n\n\\[\nt = \\frac{200}{17}\n\\]\n\nNow, we will calculate the value of \\( t \\) and round it to the nearest whole number:\n\n\\[\nt \\approx \\frac{200}{17} \\approx 11.7647\n\\]\n\nRounding 11.7647 to the nearest whole number, we get:\n\n\\[\nt \\approx 12\n\\]\n\nSo, it will take approximately 12 minutes to print 200 pages. We can verify this using Python code.\n```python\n# Given values\npages_per_minute = 17\ntotal_pages = 200\n\n# Calculate the time in minutes\ntime_minutes = total_pages / pages_per_minute\n\n# Round to the nearest whole number\ntime_minutes_rounded = round(time_minutes)\nprint(time_minutes_rounded)\n```\n```output\n12\n```\nThe calculations confirm that it will take approximately \\(\\boxed{12}\\) minutes to print 200 pages.",
